(1) Escape Character:-The escape characters in Python – special sequences that start with a backslash \ and
represent characters that are hard to type or have special meaning.

To insert characters that are illegal in a string, use an escape character.
An escape character is a backslash \ followed by the character you want to insert.

(2) Common Escape Characters:-

Escape Sequence	Meaning	Example	Output
\'	Single quote	print('It\'s nice')	It's nice
\"	Double quote	print("He said \"Hi\"")	He said "Hi"
\\	Backslash	print("C:\\Users\\Name")	C:\Users\Name
\n	New line	print("Hello\nWorld")	Hello
World
\r	Carriage return	print("Hello\rWorld")	World (overwrites)
\t	Tab	print("Hello\tWorld")	Hello World
\b	Backspace	print("Hello\bWorld")	HellWorld (deletes 'o')
\f	Form feed	print("Hello\fWorld")	(page break, rarely used)
\ooo	Octal value (o = 0-7)	print("\110\145\154\154\157")	Hello (ASCII values)
\xhh	Hex value (h = 0-9, A-F)	print("\x48\x65\x6c\x6c\x6f")	Hello
